<%#
# Notice: two-factor authentication is off

Shown on «Сводка» to a super admin whose user has no two-factor authentication: the sign-in to this console is protected
by the password alone, and the notice says where to turn the second step on (the profile of the user in the operator app).
Nothing is forced: a super admin without it still signs in with the password. When the server has no encryption keys the
second step cannot be enabled at all, and the notice says that instead.

## Local variables:

- `super_admin`: the signed-in super admin.
%>
<% unless super_admin.mfa_enabled? %>
  <section class="mb-5 flex flex-col gap-1.5 rounded-xl bg-n-amber-2 px-4 py-3 text-sm text-n-amber-11 outline outline-1 -outline-offset-1 outline-n-amber-4" role="status" data-testid="two-factor-notice">
    <h2 class="m-0 text-heading-3 text-n-amber-11"><%= t('super_admin.two_factor.notice.title') %></h2>
    <p class="m-0"><%= t(Chatwoot.mfa_enabled? ? 'super_admin.two_factor.notice.how_to' : 'super_admin.two_factor.notice.unavailable') %></p>
    <% if Chatwoot.mfa_enabled? %>
      <p class="m-0">
        <%= link_to t('super_admin.two_factor.notice.open_app'), app_path, class: 'font-medium text-n-amber-11 underline' %>
      </p>
    <% end %>
  </section>
<% end %>
